# Platypus-Bear: with no Lesson card in your graveyard it keeps defender (CR 702.3b). Its enter trigger mills two Plains, so on turn 3 it can't
# be declared as an attacker while Bot1's Memnite can (Bot2 20 -> 19). Bot2's Firebending Lesson, aimed at the Bear on turn 2, ends up in
# Bot2's graveyard, not Bot1's, and the 2 damage doesn't kill the 2/3 Bear: it still can't attack. (The other half is in the scenario
# where a milled Lesson lets it attack.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Platypus-Bear
Memnite
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Firebending Lesson
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Platypus-Bear.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Plains; Plains
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Firebending Lesson.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Platypus-Bear)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
? Bot2.Graveyard = Firebending Lesson
? Bot1.Battlefield = Memnite; Mox Emerald; Mox Ruby; Platypus-Bear
! Bot1.Attack(Platypus-Bear > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
